_AMC_12_Q14_m1","label":"Find the distance from the center to the chord","methodDirectNodeIds":{"1982_AMC_12_Q14_m1":["cnm_262","cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_251","cnm_174","cnm_h180"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_262","cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_251","cnm_174","cnm_h180","cnm_250","cnm_260","cnm_064","cnm_055","cnm_075"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B. 21","reason":"The side lengths give BD=5 and AD=12. Set D=(0,0), A=(0,12), B=(-5,0), C=(9,0). Since DE is perpendicular to AC, write F=(4t,3t). Then AF perpendicular to BF gives (4t,3t-12) dot (4t+5,3t)=t(25t-16)=0. As F differs from D, t=16/25 and DF=5t=16/5. This lies within DE=36/5, and m+n=21.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2013_AMC_12B_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"diameter-circle-chord","label":"Diameter circle and chord","methodDirectNodeIds":{"diameter-circle-chord":["cnm_254","cnm_h174","cnm_h180"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_254","cnm_h174","cnm_h180"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: 3","reason":"The expanded circle equations are x^2 + y^2 + 20x + 8y - 53 = 0 and x^2 + y^2 - 6x - 18y + 25 = 0. Subtracting gives 26x + 26y - 78 = 0, so x + y = 3 and c = 3.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2017_AMC_12B_Q09","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"equal-common-chord-lengths","label":"Equate the common chord lengths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"equal-common-chord-lengths":["cnm_h174","cnm_h180","cnm_042"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h174","cnm_h180","cnm_042"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: 11","reason":"The condition is (x - 5)^2 + (-x - 5)^2 <= 100, which simplifies to 2x^2 + 50 <= 100. Thus -5 <= x <= 5, giving 11 integers including both endpoints.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canon